; Axis C (exclusive-group presence) — group-aware rule, masking case.
;
; The author writes `:at`; `:from` has a literal default of 0. With
; the group-aware rule (production), `:at` is author-present, so the
; sibling defaulted `:from` is dropped from the presence count ->
; exactly-one satisfied, clean.
;
; This is the fixture that motivated the rule: with unconditional
; default-presence (the held-off behavior) `:from`'s overlay default
; would have triggered `mutually_exclusive_keys_present` here. The
; group-aware rule treats author choices as authoritative.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name track
    (key :name at :type number :optional true)
    (key :name from :type number :default 0 :optional true)
    (exclusive-group :cardinality exactly-one
      (alt :keys [at])
      (alt :keys [from]))))

(track :at 12)
